{"id":"a2f9c43ff970dfe4","group":"58","path":"58/batch03/58-thm-hausdorff-formula.md","title":"Hausdorff Formula","display":"thm-hausdorff-formula — Hausdorff Formula","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-thm-hausdorff-formula","aliases":["58-thm-hausdorff-formula","Hausdorff Recursion Formula"],"display":"thm-hausdorff-formula — Hausdorff Formula","depends_on":["[[58-df-aleph]]","[[58-df-cofinality]]","[[58-df-cardinalexpp]]","[[58-df-gch]]","[[58-thm-aleph-properties]]","[[58-thm-konig]]","[[58-df-ordinal]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-thm-hausdorff-formula"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-thm-hausdorff-formula</span><span>Hausdorff Recursion Formula</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-hausdorff-formula — Hausdorff Formula"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"535817bf563314f5\" href=\"?note=535817bf563314f5\" title=\"58-df-aleph\">58-df-aleph</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"315ad00b8744fdfc\" href=\"?note=315ad00b8744fdfc\" title=\"58-df-cofinality\">58-df-cofinality</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"949691fe1747f59d\" href=\"?note=949691fe1747f59d\" title=\"58-df-cardinalexpp\">58-df-cardinalexpp</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"f13d4bbe06c4eb5a\" href=\"?note=f13d4bbe06c4eb5a\" title=\"58-df-gch\">58-df-gch</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"a4742eae48926358\" href=\"?note=a4742eae48926358\" title=\"58-thm-aleph-properties\">58-thm-aleph-properties</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"b2477134b6aa9c7a\" href=\"?note=b2477134b6aa9c7a\" title=\"58-thm-konig\">58-thm-konig</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-7\" data-note=\"5582a281f15a33c2\" href=\"?note=5582a281f15a33c2\" title=\"58-df-ordinal\">58-df-ordinal</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\alpha,\\beta\\in V\">\\(\\alpha,\\beta\\in V\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{GCH}\\in\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(\\mathrm{GCH}\\in\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span> (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-8\" data-note=\"f13d4bbe06c4eb5a\" href=\"?note=f13d4bbe06c4eb5a\" title=\"58-df-gch\">58-df-gch</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Ordinal}:V\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(\\mathrm{Ordinal}:V\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{cf}:V\\to V\">\\(\\mathrm{cf}:V\\to V\\)</span> (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-9\" data-note=\"5582a281f15a33c2\" href=\"?note=5582a281f15a33c2\" title=\"58-df-ordinal\">58-df-ordinal</a> and <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-10\" data-note=\"315ad00b8744fdfc\" href=\"?note=315ad00b8744fdfc\" title=\"58-df-cofinality\">58-df-cofinality</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}hausdorff\\text{-}formula} \\vdash\n\\mathrm{GCH}\\land\\mathrm{Ordinal}(\\alpha)\\land\\mathrm{Ordinal}(\\beta)\\land\n\\aleph_\\beta&lt;\\mathrm{cf}(\\aleph_\\alpha)\n\\to\\aleph_\\alpha^{\\aleph_\\beta}=\\aleph_\\alpha\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}hausdorff\\text{-}formula} \\vdash\n\\mathrm{GCH}\\land\\mathrm{Ordinal}(\\alpha)\\land\\mathrm{Ordinal}(\\beta)\\land\n\\aleph_\\beta&lt;\\mathrm{cf}(\\aleph_\\alpha)\n\\to\\aleph_\\alpha^{\\aleph_\\beta}=\\aleph_\\alpha\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>This is the central formula of cardinal arithmetic below <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\aleph_\\omega\">\\(\\aleph_\\omega\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>The case <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\aleph_\\beta &lt; \\mathrm{cf}(\\aleph_\\alpha)\">\\(\\aleph_\\beta &lt; \\mathrm{cf}(\\aleph_\\alpha)\\)</span> is the cofinality restriction.</li>\n<li>Other cases express <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\aleph_\\alpha^{\\aleph_\\beta}\">\\(\\aleph_\\alpha^{\\aleph_\\beta}\\)</span> in terms of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\aleph_{\\alpha+1}\">\\(\\aleph_{\\alpha+1}\\)</span> or <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"2^{\\aleph_\\beta}\">\\(2^{\\aleph_\\beta}\\)</span> according to the position of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\aleph_\\beta\">\\(\\aleph_\\beta\\)</span> relative to <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{cf}(\\aleph_\\alpha)\">\\(\\mathrm{cf}(\\aleph_\\alpha)\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>Under GCH, the formula becomes much simpler.</li>\n<li>Foundation for computing cardinal exponentiation.</li>\n<li>Also known as the &quot;Hausdorff recursion formula&quot; for computing <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\aleph_\\alpha^{\\aleph_\\beta}\">\\(\\aleph_\\alpha^{\\aleph_\\beta}\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>Ordinal parameters are guarded by the sourced unary predicate; the proper class <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Ord}\">\\(\\mathrm{Ord}\\)</span> is not treated as a set-valued quantifier domain.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-aleph","status":"resolved","id":"535817bf563314f5","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-aleph]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-cofinality","status":"resolved","id":"315ad00b8744fdfc","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-cofinality]]","embed":false},{"target":"